*  THE ORIGINAL IS CLI SEGPAGE+3,SEGINV -- AN EQUALITY TEST,   XA0036DK         
*  NOT A BIT TEST. BYTE 3 EQUALS SEGINV EXACTLY ONLY WHEN THE  XA0036DK         
*  PTO'S LOW BYTE IS ZERO AND THE INVALID FLAG IS SET, WHICH   XA0036DK         
*  IS THE 'NEVER BUILT' CASE. THE NEXT TWO CARDS THEN          XA0036DK         
*  SEPARATE A SECOND CASE -- BUILT BUT INVALID, MIGRATING --   XA0036DK         
*  AND THAT IS THE ONE THE TRANS AT 00962000 EXISTS TO WAIT    XA0036DK         
*  FOR. CONVERTING THIS TO TM COLLAPSED THE TWO INTO ONE: ANY  XA0036DK         
*  INVALID ENTRY TOOK NEXTSEG, SO REACHING 00958000 MEANT THE  XA0036DK         
*  BIT WAS CLEAR, BZ WAS ALWAYS TAKEN, AND THE TRANS BECAME    XA0036DK         
*  DEAD CODE. THE EQUALITY TEST SURVIVES THE CONVERSION        XA0036DK         
*  UNCHANGED IN KIND -- ONLY THE CONSTANT MOVES, BECAUSE AN    XA0036DK         
*  UNBUILT ESA/390 STE READS X'20': INVALID WITH PTL ZERO,     XA0036DK         
